{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>May terror fall upon them.</b> It is a petition — may it dwell upon them and may the dread not depart from them; like the expression ועל פני כל אחיו נפל, 'and he fell before all his brothers.'" "<b>In the greatness of Your arm.</b> Like בזרוע גדלך, 'in the arm of Your greatness'; the pattern is like קדוש היכלך, which is like היכל קדשך, 'the sanctuary of Your holiness.'" "<b>Until Your people pass, זו — You acquired.</b> Whom You acquired for Yourself by bringing them out of the land of Egypt — until You bring them and plant them on the mount of Your inheritance. <b>זו:</b> in place of אשר."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:02.858253205Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}